# OpenHarth Agent Skill

Use OpenHarth CLI/API to audit GitHub contributions, explain hidden repos, compare users, and publish shareable reports.

## Commands
- `openhearth audit <user> --month YYYY-MM --ai-summary`
- `openhearth hidden <user> --month YYYY-MM --ai-explain`
- `openhearth proof <user> --month YYYY-MM --ai-summary`
- `openhearth overlap <userA> <userB> --month YYYY-MM`
- `openhearth lens <user> <owner/repo> --year YYYY`
- `openhearth agent run_audit --username <user> --month YYYY-MM`
- `openhearth agent ask_summary --username <user> --month YYYY-MM --ai-tone hiring`
- `openhearth mcp --port 9455`

## Rules
- Default tone: neutral. Use hiring/technical/exec only when explicitly requested.
- For gist/webhook writes, require explicit `--approve` or user confirmation.
- Never expose tokens in logs or summaries.
